        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "94461374-c9b5-5dfb-aa77-e0563a55c11c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lester James Peries, Jean Vigo, Ravindra Randeniya, Malini Fonseka\n- Roles: film director, screenwriter, film producer\n- Films: Rekava, Gamperaliya, Nidhanaya, Golu Hadawatha, Kaliyugaya, Awaragira, Yuganthaya, Wekande Walauwa\n- Concepts: Sinhala Cinema, poetic realism, French New Wave\n- Places: Sri Lanka, France\n\nFacts:\n- Jean Vigo was a French film director born on 26 April 1905 and died on 5 October 1934.\n- Jean Vigo helped establish poetic realism in film in the 1930s and posthumously influenced the French New Wave of the late 1950s and early 1960s.\n- Lester James Peries was born on 5 April 1919 and became an internationally acclaimed Sri Lankan film director, screenwriter, and film producer.\n- Lester James Peries had been an active filmmaker since 1949 and was involved in more than 28 films, including shorts and documentaries.\n- Lester James Peries received critical acclaim for directing Rekava, Gamperaliya, Nidhanaya, Golu Hadawatha, Kaliyugaya, Awaragira, and Yuganthaya.\n- Lester James Peries often made films about Sri Lankan family life in rural settings and conflicted characters, and he helped create an authentic expression of Sinhala Cinema.\n- Wekande Walauwa, a film by Lester James Peries starring Ravindra Randeniya and Malini Fonseka, was Sri Lanka's first submission for the Academy Awards.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
